  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2024-2025 American International College 'Program Plan' for General Business (School of Business, Arts and Sciences). Semester totals printed on the plan: 15x8 = 120 credits (TOTAL CREDITS: 120). The program is a Bachelor of Science in Business Administration (BSBA) per the official aic.edu program page. 'Business or related field course' slots 1-7 (21 credits) fulfill the major's field-concentration requirement: nine credits of 2000-level or higher courses in a single business or related field other than management, nine credits in a second single business or related field other than management, and three credits in any business field. Eligible fields: Accounting; Arts and Entertainment Management (any AEM course 2000-level or higher); Cybersecurity; Economics/Finance; Entrepreneurship (MKT3510, MKT3550, MKT3656); Esports Management and Administration; Healthcare Management; International Business; Marketing; Sports and Recreation Management. Junior Fall 'MGT3201 Business and Society or MGT3201 Leadership' is transcribed as printed on the plan (both options show the same number). The capstone is MGT4800 Senior Policy Seminar OR BUS4899 Business Internship (one in Senior Fall, the other in Senior Spring — both are Common Professional Component requirements, transcribed as printed). General Education categories per the 2024-2025 plan: Cat 1 Scientific World (math + science with lab), Cat 2 Self and Others, Cat 3 Interdisciplinarity (ENG1202 + INT courses), Cat 4 Arts and Humanities, Cat 5 Professional Readiness (AIC1005/AIC1100 + AIC3005). tccns mirrors the local course code (AIC is in Massachusetts; no TCCNS). transfer_confidence is 'core_only'.",
